# Citation File Format — https://citation-file-format.github.io
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file.
#
# TODO before the next release: publish a datapin release to Zenodo (using
# datapin) and add the resulting concept DOI here as `doi:` under
# `identifiers:`, plus the badge in README.md. See issue #54 §5.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "datapin: pin, sync, and publish research data"
message: "If you used datapin to publish or version research data, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  datapin is a single-binary Go CLI for FAIR research-data publication. It
  groups files into a dataset in a committed manifest and publishes them to an
  archive repository (Zenodo or any InvenioRDM instance, Dataverse, Figshare)
  as an immutable, versioned, DOI-carrying record — or syncs the same dataset
  to a journal-versioned workspace remote (directory, S3, SFTP) when it is not
  yet ready for a DOI. Every file is pinned to an exact version and checksum,
  and any layer that can contradict that pin fails loudly rather than
  delivering different bytes.
authors:
